# Git, secrets, and proof

## Owner gates

| Action | Default |
|--------|---------|
| Commit | Only when owner asks |
| Push | Only when owner asks |
| Deploy / release / prod migration | Only explicit “yes” |
| Schema / new dependency | Only explicit “yes” |

Never `--no-verify`, force-push main, or amend others’ commits.

## Secrets

Never add `.env` production secrets, Firebase admin JSON, shared activation codes, real customer PII dumps, or foreign-project credentials to git.

## Noise to exclude from commits

Unless owner asks: local `reports/*-pass*.txt`, stress logs, accidental report trims, Playwright `test-results/`, ad-hoc eval scripts not part of the agreed deliverable.

## Final answer shape (after implementation)

- **What** changed (user-visible behavior)
- **Why** (ops problem)
- **Security** (RBAC / tenant / credentials / conflict)
- **Proof** (commands + exit codes)
- **Files** touched
- **Risk** / **Not done**

If unproven, say so — never claim “done” or “deployed” without evidence.
